* The vessel diameter to place the AngioGuard™ device in must be \> 3 and \ 50% and \ 50% stenosis;
* Patient has an ostial target lesion;
* Significant (\>50%) untreated stenosis proximal or distal to the target lesion that will be treated during the procedure, since this may require revascularization or impede runoff;
* Ejection fraction \<30%;
* Totally occluded vessel (TIMI 0 Level).

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Understands and voluntarily signs the informed consent form (ICF);
2. Age ≥18 years;
3. Histopathologically confirmed plasmablastic lymphoma (PBL);
4. Positive BCMA or GPRC5D expression: BCMA or GPRC5D expression on tumor cells confirmed by immunohistochemistry (IHC) or flow cytometry;
5. Treatment-naive or having received no more than 1 cycle of prior systemic therapy (e.g., CHOP, EPOCH);
6. Measurable disease (unless only bone marrow lesions are present), defined as at least one lesion with a longest diameter ≥1.5 cm as measured by CT or PET-CT;
7. ECOG performance status 0-2 (may be relaxed to 3 for elderly/frail patients if organ function permits);
8. Liver function tests meeting the following criteria: total bilirubin ≤1.5× upper limit of normal (ULN), unless due to Gilbert's syndrome or of non-hepatic origin; aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ≤3×ULN (except for liver function impairment caused by tumor invasion);
9. Renal function tests meeting the following criterion: creatinine clearance ≥30 mL/min (calculated using the Cockcroft-Gault formula);
10. Blood routine tests within 14 days before the start of screening meeting the following criteria (except in patients with bone marrow involvement): absolute neutrophil count ≥1.0×10⁹/L and platelet count ≥75×10⁹/L; Expected life expectancy ≥2 months as judged by the investigator.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Diagnosis or treatment of a malignancy other than PBL within 1 year before enrollment (except for cases treated with surgery alone and considered cured);
2. Prior autologous or allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation (HSCT) or CAR-T therapy;
3. History of epilepsy or other central nervous system disorders;
4. Other severe medical conditions that could affect the study (e.g., myocardial infarction within 6 months, uncontrolled diabetes, other severe cardiopulmonary diseases, etc.); the determination is at the investigator's discretion;
5. Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection;
6. Active hepatitis B virus (HBV) or hepatitis C virus (HCV) infection, defined as HBV-DNA or HCV-RNA above the upper limit of detection, with or without abnormal liver function. If a patient had active HBV infection at initial diagnosis and converted to inactive HBV infection after anti-HBV treatment, the patient may be enrolled in this study provided adequate anti-HBV therapy;
7. Pregnant or lactating women, or women of childbearing potential not using contraceptive measures;
8. Major surgery (e.g., requiring general anesthesia) within 2 weeks before enrollment, or not expected to fully recover from surgery, or surgery planned during the planned study participation period. Note: subjects with planned surgical procedures under local anesthesia may participate in the study;
9. Hypersensitivity to the drugs used;
10. Any active severe psychiatric illness, medical illness, or other symptoms/conditions that, as judged by the investigator, may affect treatment, compliance, or the ability to provide informed consent.

Inclusion Criteria:

* males and females aged \>18 years;
* established diagnosis of adrenal insufficiency in congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency;
* stably treated with conventional glucocorticoids, available to change their regimen according to random allocation
* written informed consent/assent to participate in the study in compliance with local regulations.

Exclusion Criteria:

* clinical or laboratory signs of severe cerebral, respiratory, hepatobiliary or pancreatic diseases, renal dysfunction, gastrointestinal emptying, or motility disturbances (i.e. chronic diarrhea), significant psychiatric illnesses;
* history of/or current alcohol and/or drug abuse;
* night shift workers;
* underlying diseases that could necessitate treatment with glucocorticoids;
* therapies with hepatic enzyme induction drugs interfering with glucocorticoid kinetics, or immunosuppressive steroid therapy;
* patients with a documented intolerance/known hypersensitivity to dual release hydrocortisone;
* vulnerable populations, such as elderly, cancer patients, pregnant and lactating women;
* history of non-compliance to medical regimens, or potentially unreliable patients

简要说明:
The objective of the clinical study is to evaluate the tolerability, safety, immunogenicity and prophylactic efficacy of the EpiVacCorona vaccine in volunteers aged 18 and above.

The study tasks are to:

* evaluate the safety of the EpiVacCorona vaccine when administered twice intramuscularly;
* evaluate the tolerability of the EpiVacCorona vaccine when administered twice intramuscularly;
* identify any adverse events to the administration of the EpiVacCorona vaccine;
* investigate the humoral immune response following two doses of the EpiVacCorona vaccine;
* investigate the cell-mediated immune response following two doses of the EpiVacCorona vaccine;
* evaluate the prophylactic efficacy of the EpiVacCorona vaccine when administered twice intramuscularly.

